From: Andrea <26578395+m0s4ik@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: count depth/stencil MSAA samples once in GMEM sizing

gmem_key_init() multiplies the depth/stencil resource's layout.cpp by the
framebuffer's sample count, but layout.cpp already includes the resource's
samples (fd5_layout and the other fdl layouts do cpp *= nr_samples). With
4x MSAA a 4-byte Z24S8 buffer is counted as 64 bytes per pixel instead of
16, even the smallest bin no longer fits in GMEM, and calc_nbins() keeps
adding bins forever: the process spins at 100% in layout_gmem().

Take the bytes of one sample from the format and multiply by the
framebuffer's samples once, as the color buffers already do.

Seen on the Adreno 506 (Lenovo ThinkSmart View) with WPE WebKit and Qt
WebEngine, which draw with 4x MSAA. Root cause found by lzl51230
(https://github.com/rickx/ubuntu-thinksmart/pull/5).

---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -495,9 +495,16 @@
 
    if (has_zs || assume_zs) {
       struct fd_resource *rsc = fd_resource(pfb->zsbuf.texture);
-      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] = rsc->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+      /* layout.cpp already includes the resource's sample count: take the
+       * bytes of one sample from the format and count the framebuffer's
+       * samples once, like the color buffers below.
+       */
+      key->zsbuf_cpp[0] =
+         util_format_get_blocksize(rsc->layout.format) * pfb->samples;
       if (rsc->stencil)
-         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] = rsc->stencil->layout.cpp * pfb->samples;
+         key->zsbuf_cpp[1] =
+            util_format_get_blocksize(rsc->stencil->layout.format) *
+            pfb->samples;
 
       /* If we clear z or s but not both, and we are using z24s8 (ie.
        * !separate_stencil) then we need to restore the other, even if
